      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "If we assume that the math books are A, B, and C, and the English books are D, E, F, G, H, then there are only 2 possibilities for the arrangement:  ABCDEFGH or  ABCFEHDG.  There are $2\\times3!=24$ different arrangements of the math books and $2\\times 4!=24$ different arrangements of the English books, so the total number of arrangements is $24\\cdot 24=\\boxed{576}$. \nNote:  This assumes that all the books are of different genres.",
